Repairs Complete: Entertainment Video Feed & Layout in THE LIGHT OF AKWA IBOM
Root Cause Identified & Repaired
Network Video Stream Blockage: The previous sample URLs were hosted on a restricted storage bucket returning HTTP 403 Forbidden, causing the player to fail silently.
Legacy SurfaceView Conflict: The original implementation relied on legacy Android VideoView which suffers from surface detachment and black screens inside Jetpack Compose VerticalPager.
Missing Buffering State: There was no buffering listener or loading indicator to inform users that video data was downloading.
Edge-to-Edge Overlap: Missing WindowInsets padding caused the top branding bar to collide with the phone camera notch/status bar, and the bottom navigation to collide with Android's system navigation buttons (exit, home, and minimize).
Key Improvements Implemented
Integrated Media3 ExoPlayer (androidx.media3):
Replaced legacy VideoView with Google's official Media3 ExoPlayer and PlayerView with RESIZE_MODE_ZOOM for true vertical full-screen playback.
Auto-Play & Auto-Pause: Immediately when a video is visible, it starts playing automatically without tapping. When the user swipes to the next video, the previous video pauses instantly.
Smooth Buffering Indicator: Centered circular loading spinner (LightSunGold) displays while media buffers, ensuring transparent and smooth loading.
One-Tap Play/Pause: Tapping anywhere on the video toggles playback with an animated on-screen indicator.
Genuine Working Video Content (Africa, China, Philippines):
Updated with verified, fast-streaming HTTP 200 OK MP4 CDN video feeds:
Akwa Ibom & African: Cultural Ekombi dance celebration in Uyo, Nollywood short movies, and Afrobeats festival clips.
Chinese: Wushu Kung Fu martial arts action, Sichuan Bian Lian face-changing opera, and dragon festival celebrations.
Philippine: Acoustic Harana serenade, Cebu street festival, and island music.
Category Filters: Top filter chips allow instant switching between All, African, Chinese, Philippine, and Akwa Ibom.
Complete TikTok-Style Overlays:
Like Button (Heart): Real-time like counter with fill animation.
Comments Drawer: Interactive bottom sheet displaying discussions and allowing instant comment posting.
Native Share Button: Native Android share chooser with video title and branding.
Follow Button: + badge on creator avatar toggles follow state.
Audio Disc: Rotating vinyl disc with sound title and mute/unmute audio toggle.
Video Upload: Floating Action Button allowing users to upload their own videos.
Screen Insets & Safe Area Fixed:
Upper Screen: Added statusBarsPadding() to LightTopBar to push the logo, "THE LIGHT OF AKWA IBOM", and slogan "“BRIGHTER WE SHINE!”" down below the phone's camera cutout, clock, and status bar.
Lower Screen: Added navigationBarsPadding() to LightBottomNav to lift all tabs and badges up so they never overlap Android's exit, home, or minimize system navigation buttons.
"GET STARTED" Onboarding Flow:
The app now opens with a welcoming GET STARTED screen showcasing your uploaded logo, cultural greeting, and overview of all sections.
Tapping the prominent "GET STARTED" button launches directly into the TikTok video feed where the first entertaining video starts playing automatically.
Pressing Android's back button from the home video feed safely returns to the Get Started screen without closing the app.
Friendly Offline Handling:
If internet connectivity drops, the app displays a friendly offline screen with a Retry Connection button rather than a blank screen.
